# Wajiha UI library

- Inspect `com.wajiha.ui.components` and `.gamepad` before building UI. Refine an existing primitive when behavior fits; add a shared primitive only for a proven reusable gap. Do not create parallel settings APIs, one-off Material preference chrome, custom focus rings, or duplicate gamepad key handling.
- Canonical settings composition: `WajihaScreen` → `WajihaFolderSettingChrome` (Settings gutters via `WajihaFolderChromeMetrics`) → section content with public `Wajiha*Setting`/field/action components → shared hints and hero publication. Do not hand-roll Back + `FolderTabRow` + `WajihaSettingPanel` or use `md` horizontal padding for folder windows.
- Prefer `GamepadSettingRow` and public `Wajiha*Setting` wrappers, including expandable, color-choice, value, dual-action, field-message, trailing-action, and focus-restoration APIs. Use `GamepadButton`, `GamepadChip`, `GamepadSafeTextField`, wrapped Switch/Slider controls, and shared empty/loading/error/dialog components instead of raw equivalents. Chrome min height is `SettingsCompactRowMinHeight` / `LocalSettingRowMinHeight` (44.dp) — Back, folder tabs, and setting rows share that standard.
- Preserve interaction semantics: A primary; X contextual secondary (for example Menu, Edit, or Remove); Y reset only when supported and non-default; B exits edit/collapses before back; L1/R1 changes sections. Touch gets deliberate one-tap parity without duplicate nested actions.
- Text fields follow `Idle` → `Selected` → `Editing`: navigation selects without opening the IME, touch or A explicitly edits, and B exits editing while restoring the navigation anchor. Recomposition, filtering, validation, and value updates must not steal focus.
- Explain disabled controls, restore focus after dialogs/navigation, and define whether each row publishes dual-display hero state or intentionally does not. Defaults, overrides, reset visibility, parsing, persistence, and destructive confirmation must match the model/repository contract.
- Exceptions: `GamepadTile`, system overlays, context menus, onboarding/review workflows with an intentional separate UI family, and anything under `Study/`.
- Before handoff: search for an existing primitive, avoid parallel APIs, verify defaults/reset/persistence, run formatting/build checks, and test affected gamepad and dual-display flows on Thor.
